org.apache.streampipes.connectors.s3.object.title=S3 Object Storage
org.apache.streampipes.connectors.s3.object.description=Reads objects from S3 and S3-compatible object storage such as MinIO or SeaweedFS
endpoint-url.title=Endpoint URL
endpoint-url.description=Base URL of the S3 API, for example https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com or http://minio:9000
region.title=Region
region.description=Region the bucket belongs to, for example eu-central-1. S3-compatible stores usually accept us-east-1
access-key.title=Access key
access-key.description=Access key ID used to authenticate against the endpoint
secret-key.title=Secret key
secret-key.description=Secret access key used to authenticate against the endpoint
bucket.title=Bucket
bucket.description=Name of the bucket to read objects from
object-pattern.title=Object pattern
object-pattern.description=Glob matched against the object key, for example json/sensors-*.json. The leading literal part is pushed down to the server as a prefix
after-read.title=After read
after-read.description=What happens to an object once it has been read. The keep options leave the bucket untouched and remember which objects were processed; move and delete modify the bucket but need no state
keep-persistent.title=Keep objects (tracked on disk)
keep-persistent.description=Leaves the bucket untouched and remembers processed objects on disk. Needs a persistent volume to survive a restart
keep-in-memory.title=Keep objects (tracked in memory)
keep-in-memory.description=Leaves the bucket untouched, but forgets what it processed when the adapter restarts, so everything is ingested again
move.title=Move objects to another bucket
move.description=Copies each object to an archive bucket and removes it from the source bucket. Needs PutObject and DeleteObject permissions
delete.title=Delete objects
delete.description=Deletes each object from the bucket after it has been read. Needs DeleteObject permission
archive-group.title=Archive settings
archive-group.description=Where moved objects are placed
archive-bucket.title=Archive bucket
archive-bucket.description=Bucket that objects are moved to once they have been read
poll-interval-ms.title=Poll interval (ms)
poll-interval-ms.description=How often the bucket is listed for new objects
